xnu 0227: cache maintenance that happens, and a probe for a black panel

XNU is built with __ARM_COHERENT_IO__ on arm64 (pexpert/pexpert/arm64/
apple_arm64_common.h), and in that build flush_dcache() and clean_dcache() are
a bare dsb sy (osfmk/arm/caches.c): they order, they never clean. Every flush
this port asked for was therefore a no-op, including 0222's command-stream
writeback and the ring range clean whose page offset 0225 then fixed. Nothing
on this board is IO-coherent -- the panel reads DRAM and the Adreno reads DRAM
behind the CPU caches -- so mondrian_gpu_uc_flush() does the work itself now:
dc civac a line at a time, the line size from CTR_EL0, through the physmap
alias of the page, then a dsb sy. ios-topaz reached the same conclusion twice
over (0111 there: "this kernel is built with the Apple SoC config
(__ARM_COHERENT_IO__), where clean_dcache/flush_dcache are no-ops").

The framebuffer reads a surface through its own Normal Non-Cacheable mapping
while the process that draws holds a cacheable one of the same pages
(MondrianSurface::kernelAddress() against MondrianSurface.cpp's mapCache), so
it cleans and drops those lines before it copies: mondrianfb_nocoh=1 turns
that off for the A/B, and mondrianfb_probe=N says what the surface held and
what the copy left, which is how a panel that goes black at the first swap is
told apart from a copy that never ran.

